content.text:
Fix the real checkpoint audit so it can use intent safely. Work only in the checkpoint-audit collector boundary and its focused tests; do not change the evaluator privacy contract, Gemini transport, UI, or unrelated code.

The collector may read raw checkpoint intent locally, but it must derive a bounded typed `SanitizedRequirement` list before constructing `intentlens.EvidencePackage`. The evaluator/Gemini request must still be structurally unable to receive raw prompts, transcripts, logs, arbitrary JSON, or raw patches.

Implement conservative local sanitization:

* extract short atomic requirement candidates from developer intent;
* remove/skip candidates containing secrets, tokens, credentials, or transcript-like content;
* cap count and length;
